// 26 U.S.C. Subtitle I — Trust Fund Code (Chapter 98, §§9500-9511, plus the
// Chapter 98 Subchapter B management sections §§9601-9602). The text is
// pinned whole (`sources.law`, generated from the shared Title 26 snapshot,
// `sync_us_irc_fragments.py --package trust-funds`); modules below
// formalize it.
//
// MODULE MAP
//   package.law                        — shared ontology, imports, type aliases (this file)
//   00-shared.law                      — §9500 short title; the fund/tax-linkage/
//                                         expenditure/borrowing/claims-limited shapes
//                                         every individual fund module reuses
//   01-black-lung-9501.law             — §9501 Black Lung Disability Trust Fund
//   02-airport-airway-9502.law         — §9502 Airport and Airway Trust Fund
//   03-highway-9503.law                — §9503 Highway Trust Fund + Mass Transit Account
//   04-waterborne-9504-9506.law        — §9504 Sport Fish Restoration and Boating,
//                                         §9505 Harbor Maintenance, §9506 Inland Waterways
//   05-environmental-9507-9509.law     — §9507 Hazardous Substance Superfund,
//                                         §9508 Leaking Underground Storage Tank,
//                                         §9509 Oil Spill Liability
//   06-health-9510-9511.law            — §9510 Vaccine Injury Compensation,
//                                         §9511 Patient-Centered Outcomes Research
//   07-management-9601-9602.law        — §9601 monthly transfer duty,
//                                         §9602 report/investment duties of the Secretary
//   08-highway-apportionment-stage3.law — stage 3: §9503(d)(3)-(6), (e)(4)-(5), (f)(1)
//                                         apportionment adjustments, share and balance rules
//   09-claims-order-and-adjustments-stage3.law — stage 3: order of payment of claims
//                                         (§§9507(e)(3), 9508(d)(3), 9509(e)(3), 9510(d)(3)),
//                                         §9510(c)(2)(B) estimate adjustments
//
// `us.irc.definitions` is a sibling package under construction; this stage
// does not depend on it. `us.irc.excise_goods` is NOT imported: the funding
// linkage this package models (`fund_funded_by`) names WHICH tax finances a
// fund; it does not recompute the tax amount from excise-goods' per-event
// relations (see 00-shared.law's module header for why).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.trust_funds version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:trust_funds:clir";

import us.irc.core version "0.1.1";

type Person = us.irc.core::Person;
type Organ = us.irc.core::Organ;
type Period = us.irc.core::Period;
type TaxableYear = us.irc.core::TaxableYear;
